    "tests": [
      "test/systems/naval/shiplivery.test.js"
    ],
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "With today's families no texel of an unpainted picture (her deck, spars, rigging, iron, bottom) is nearest a family's colour - every port ship's every livery was swept - so reading every picture paints the same ones. The list is kept because it is the law the owner's eye set (a family widened later must not reach her deck's grain, which it did while the families were drawn), and it spares the painter a pass over each of those pictures."
  },
